course: dictionary
lesson: 5662
title: The hard outer shell of the Earth
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Scientists have names for the parts of the Earth. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The Earth's hard outer shell, the lithosphere, is cracked into giant pieces called plates.» The clues are hard outer shell and cracked into pieces, so the lithosphere must be the hard, rocky outside of the Earth.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning in: «The Earth's hard rocky outer layer is cracked into giant pieces called plates.» It still makes sense, so the meaning fits. Now look at «The crust and the stiff top of the mantle together form the lithosphere.» The crust and the top of the mantle are two layers, and together they make the lithosphere.
explain: The word ends in -sphere, which tells you it is one of the layers around the planet. Its partners are the hydrosphere (water), the atmosphere (air) and the biosphere (living things). If you are not sure, a dictionary or your teacher can settle it.
fact: The lithosphere is the hard, rocky outer layer of the Earth.
fact: The lithosphere is the crust plus the very top part of the mantle, about 100 km thick.
fact: The lithosphere is broken into tectonic plates, which fit together like a cracked jigsaw.
fact: The plates of the lithosphere move slowly.
fact: The four spheres are: lithosphere (rock), hydrosphere (water), atmosphere (air) and biosphere (living things).
exercise: «The Earth's hard outer shell, the lithosphere, is cracked into giant pieces called plates.» What is the lithosphere? | *The hard, rocky outer layer of the Earth | The air around the planet | The liquid water in the oceans | The hot centre of the Earth
exercise: «The lithosphere is broken into about 15 large plates and many smaller ones.» Find and copy one word that names the pieces of the lithosphere. | broken | jigsaw | *plates | smaller
exercise: Which sphere means the water on Earth? | Biosphere | Atmosphere | *Hydrosphere | Lithosphere
test: The lithosphere is made of the crust and the very top part of which layer? | Core | Biosphere | *Mantle | Atmosphere
test: Which sphere means the air around the Earth? | *Atmosphere | Hydrosphere | Biosphere | Lithosphere
exam: The lithosphere's plates move slowly. What can this movement cause? | Sunny days | *Earthquakes, volcanoes and mountains | Rain and snow | Tides on the beach
